            <ArticleTitle>Simulation for Maintenance of Certification.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>893-905</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.suc.2015.04.010</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0039-6109(15)00062-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Maintenance of certification (MOC) is a process through which practitioners are able to show continuing competence in their areas of expertise. Simulation plays an increasingly important role in the assessment of students and residents, as well as in the initial practice certification for health care professionals. The use of simulation as an assessment tool in MOC has been sluggish to be universally accepted. This article discusses the role of simulation in health care education, how simulation might be effectively applied in the MOC process, and the future role of simulation in the MOC process.</AbstractText>
